{
  "$comment": [
    "The ecosystem registry: every repo, its tier, and whether CI is expected.",
    "",
    "status and ci are derived from what is ON MAIN, not from what a README",
    "claims. Several READMEs still say 'Reserved. It holds nothing but this file",
    "and a LICENSE' over a tree carrying dozens of files, and trusting that prose",
    "put two wrong statuses into this repo's first commit.",
    "",
    "  status  built     substantive files on main",
    "          reserved  README and LICENSE only, deliberately",
    "  ci      required  a red workflow here is a family-level failure",
    "          missing   substantive code with no workflow at all: a gap to close",
    "          none      nothing to verify yet, correct for a reserved repo",
    "",
    "'missing' is the entry that earns this file. Without a declared expectation,",
    "a repo with no CI and a repo whose CI was deleted print the same blank row.",
    "",
    "  conditional  workflows that run only when a precondition holds, so a",
    "               `skipped` result is their healthy state. attribute.yml",
    "               bisects a failed acceptance run: it is inert exactly when",
    "               the repo is well, and counting that as a problem trains the",
    "               reader to ignore the colour."
  ],
